hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27696","He said: Haddathana Waki', from Yunus, meaning Ibn Abi Ishaq, he said: I heard this hadith from al-Mughirah ibn Abd Allah from his father, similar to it."
"27697","Haddathana Abd al-Malik ibn Amr, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, they both said: Haddathana Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muhammad, from Sharik ibn Abd Allah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri, from his father, and his uncle Qatadah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Eat the meats of the sacrifices and store [source text truncated in index]."
"27698","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, he said: Haddathana Yazid ibn Ibrahim, he said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Sirin, narrated to me from Abu al-Alaniyah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: I came to this one, meaning his wife, and with her was meat of the sacrificial meats that she had kept, so I raised the stick against her, and she said: So-and-so came to us and informed us that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I had forbidden you to keep the meats of the sacrifices beyond three days, so eat and store."
"27699","Haddathana Yunus, he said: Haddathana Layth, from Yazid, meaning Ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, that Qatadah ibn al-Nu'man al-Zafari spoke against Quraysh as though he disparaged them, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Qatadah, do not revile Quraysh, for perhaps you will see men among them whose deeds you will despise your deed beside, and your act beside their acts, and you will envy them when you see them. Were it not that Quraysh would transgress, I would have informed them of what is theirs with Allah, mighty and majestic."
"27700","Yazid said: Ja'far ibn Abd Allah ibn Aslam heard me narrating this hadith and said: Thus Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah narrated to me from his father from his grandfather [source gives isnad fragment only; no matn preserved]."
